+# Agent Note: Session append ignorable option
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-24-session-append-ignorable-option.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Writers could not set the `SessionEvent.ignorable` envelope marker. `Session.append` accepted surface intent only, so every appended event was required-on-read, while the read side already skipped unknown-but-ignorable events. An out-of-tree plugin with domain event types therefore had no supported way to produce a log that stock harness builds can reopen: every cold resume refused with `SessionFormatUnsupportedError` because the plugin's types are outside the generated `KNOWN_SESSION_EVENT_TYPES`. The workarounds each fork durability or the log contract — monkey-patching `append`, constructing event objects outside `Session`, writing straight to a persistence backend, or keeping a parallel plugin-side event log.
+
+The [session log version mechanism note](../architecture/2026-08-10-session-log-version-mechanism.md) recorded this writer surface as deferred until its first consumer. AutoReportDSH (an out-of-tree physics-report workflow plugin persisting `autoreport/*` records) is that consumer.
+
+## Decision
+
+`Session.append(type, data, opts?)` takes one optional options parameter whose type depends on the event kind through the existing conditional variadic tuple:
+
+```ts ignore-check
+...opts: T extends SurfaceEventType ? [opts: SurfaceIntent] : [opts?: AppendOptions]
+```
+
+`AppendOptions` carries `ignorable?: true`. Surface events keep requiring `SurfaceIntent`; non-surface events may now carry the marker. The marker is copied onto the frozen log entry exactly like hand-authored fields, so seed validation, both persistence backends (JSONL rows serialize whole events; SQLite's dedicated column), the BFF wire schema, and the unknown-type read guard all behave as they already do for marked events. Nothing on the read path changed.
+
+A registration surface that would add out-of-tree types to the known vocabulary stays deferred; marked unknown events remain unknown-but-skippable, never interpreted.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- Monkey-patch `Session.prototype.append` from the plugin — rejected: forks the official write path, bypasses future core changes silently, and escapes typecheck at the exact boundary where durability is decided.
+- Construct `SessionEvent` objects outside `Session` or write through persistence directly — rejected: duplicates snapshot/validate/freeze/publish duties in a second place that can drift from the log contract.
+- Keep a separate plugin-side event log — rejected: splits the source of truth the session log owns, so projections and resume would reconcile two stores.
+- Allow `ignorable` inside `SurfaceIntent` for surface events too — rejected for now: surface events are model-visible reconstruction inputs, no consumer needs a skippable one, and widening the surface contract invites silent history loss.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Old writers are unaffected (absent marker still means required), and readers are unchanged. Out-of-repo plugins can now persist purely informational domain events that first-party builds skip safely; the cost is trusting writers to mark only genuinely lossless records, which is the same trust boundary the envelope contract always had. Focused tests cover marker round-trip through flush/load across all coordinator backends and refusal when an unmarked unknown event shares the log.
