+### `AppendOptions` — the non-surface parameter to `session.append()`
+
+```ts type-equiv
+/**
+ * Optional writer metadata for appending one NON-surface event via
+ * {@link Session.append}. Surface events take {@link SurfaceIntent} instead;
+ * the compiler rejects this parameter there.
+ */
+interface AppendOptions {
+  /**
+   * Marks the event one an unrecognized reader may skip: a log containing an
+   * event type outside the reading build's vocabulary stays openable when the
+   * event carries `true`. Writers set this only on purely informational
+   * records whose loss cannot affect reconstruction — out-of-repo plugin
+   * events are the intended users. Absent means required: a reader meeting an
+   * unrecognized type without this marker MUST refuse to reconstruct the
+   * session instead of silently dropping the event (see
+   * {@link SessionEvent.ignorable}).
+   */
+  ignorable?: true
+}
+```
+
+Optional for every non-`SurfaceEventType` event. The unknown-type guard on the persistence read path already honors the envelope's `ignorable` marker, so a log written by a harness (or out-of-tree plugin) carrying types this build has never seen stays openable when those records are marked — and still refuses loudly when they are not.
+
 ### `SessionSurface` — the live readonly surface projection
 
 `Session.surface` returns the session's stable `SessionSurface` view. The same incremental manager validates append candidates before commit and advances this projection from committed events; callers can observe membership and replacement generation but cannot invoke validation.
